WEBVTT

00:00:00.261 --> 00:00:01.548
Here's a first car loan.

00:00:02.232 --> 00:00:04.353
You borrow thirty thousand dollars for a used

00:00:04.394 --> 00:00:07.175
car, and each month interest of zero point

00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:09.357
six per cent is added, so the balance

00:00:09.417 --> 00:00:11.838
is multiplied by one point zero zero six.

00:00:12.641 --> 00:00:15.029
Then your six hundred dollar repayment comes off.

00:00:15.675 --> 00:00:16.586
So what do you owe now?

00:00:17.295 --> 00:00:19.320
And next month, will more of your six

00:00:19.341 --> 00:00:20.743
hundred dollars go towards the debt,

00:00:21.306 --> 00:00:21.565
less,

00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:22.568
or the same?

00:00:23.353 --> 00:00:23.816
Make a guess.

00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:26.946
The principal is the amount you borrow, and

00:00:26.987 --> 00:00:28.991
the balance is the amount you still owe.

00:00:29.813 --> 00:00:32.739
In a reducing-balance loan, interest is charged on

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.863
the balance you still owe, not on the

00:00:34.924 --> 00:00:35.905
amount you first borrowed.

00:00:36.627 --> 00:00:38.369
The rate is seven point two per cent

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:41.594
a year, compounded monthly, so each month's rate

00:00:42.316 --> 00:00:45.279
r is seven point two over twelve, which

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:46.841
is zero point six per cent.

00:00:47.645 --> 00:00:50.275
Each month, first the interest is added, so

00:00:50.296 --> 00:00:52.705
the balance is multiplied by one plus r.

00:00:53.352 --> 00:00:54.826
Then the repayment comes off.

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:57.996
So you now owe twenty-nine thousand five hundred

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:58.899
and eighty dollars.

00:00:59.562 --> 00:01:01.519
That one month is the whole rule.

00:01:02.162 --> 00:01:04.731
Call the balance after n months A sub

00:01:04.812 --> 00:01:07.240
n, so A zero is the thirty thousand

00:01:07.281 --> 00:01:07.742
you borrowed.

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:10.389
A rule that gives the next value from

00:01:10.430 --> 00:01:12.675
the one before is called a recurrence.

00:01:13.418 --> 00:01:16.262
Here, A sub n plus one equals one

00:01:16.363 --> 00:01:19.568
plus r, times A sub n, minus M,

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:20.310
the repayment.

00:01:21.193 --> 00:01:23.482
Without the repayment, this would just be compound

00:01:23.523 --> 00:01:23.863
interest.

00:01:24.286 --> 00:01:27.336
So a reducing-balance loan is a compound interest

00:01:27.377 --> 00:01:29.785
loan with a repayment taken off every period.

00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:32.995
And interest comes first, because the repayment is

00:01:33.056 --> 00:01:34.239
made at the end of the month.

00:01:34.936 --> 00:01:36.423
Here are three months in a table.

00:01:36.906 --> 00:01:39.076
Each row's interest is zero point six per

00:01:39.117 --> 00:01:40.564
cent of what's owed at the start.

00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:43.274
In month one, that's one hundred and eighty

00:01:43.295 --> 00:01:46.024
dollars, so the repayment pays off four hundred

00:01:46.046 --> 00:01:47.389
and twenty dollars of the debt.

00:01:48.192 --> 00:01:50.375
In month two, the balance is lower, so

00:01:50.396 --> 00:01:52.839
the interest is one hundred and seventy-seven dollars

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.725
forty-eight, leaving four hundred and twenty-two dollars fifty-two

00:01:56.846 --> 00:01:57.246
for the debt.

00:01:57.967 --> 00:02:00.308
In month three, the interest is one hundred

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:03.390
and seventy-four dollars ninety-four, rounded to the cent,

00:02:03.951 --> 00:02:06.331
and the balance falls to twenty-eight thousand, seven

00:02:06.372 --> 00:02:07.952
hundred and thirty-two dollars forty-two.

00:02:09.335 --> 00:02:11.385
So, each month, a little more of the

00:02:11.426 --> 00:02:12.993
repayment goes towards the debt.

00:02:13.476 --> 00:02:16.081
The repayment stays the same, but the interest

00:02:16.183 --> 00:02:18.527
is charged on a smaller balance each time.

00:02:19.109 --> 00:02:21.132
Less interest means more of the six hundred

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:23.878
dollars is left to reduce the balance, and

00:02:23.899 --> 00:02:25.982
that makes the next balance smaller again.

00:02:26.726 --> 00:02:29.060
This works because six hundred dollars is more

00:02:29.142 --> 00:02:29.765
than the interest.

00:02:30.248 --> 00:02:32.074
If it weren't, the balance wouldn't fall.

00:02:32.878 --> 00:02:34.445
Now run all five years.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:36.899
By the end, the interest is only a

00:02:37.001 --> 00:02:37.906
few dollars a month.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.758
The sixtieth repayment is just three hundred and

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.670
seventy-four dollars eighty-one, and the car is paid

00:02:43.731 --> 00:02:43.831
off.

00:02:44.817 --> 00:02:46.893
Now find the pattern behind the table.

00:02:47.617 --> 00:02:50.247
A one is thirty thousand times one point

00:02:50.268 --> 00:02:52.316
zero zero six, minus six hundred.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:55.183
For A two, multiply all of that by

00:02:55.285 --> 00:02:57.348
one point zero zero six, then take off

00:02:57.409 --> 00:02:58.330
another six hundred.

00:02:58.873 --> 00:03:01.236
That's thirty thousand times one point zero zero

00:03:01.257 --> 00:03:04.241
six squared, minus six hundred times one point

00:03:04.263 --> 00:03:06.446
zero zero six, minus six hundred.

00:03:07.409 --> 00:03:09.495
In A three, the loan has grown for

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:10.077
three months.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.483
The first repayment has been off the balance

00:03:12.505 --> 00:03:14.629
for two months, so it has stopped two

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:15.371
months of interest.

00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:17.470
The last has stopped none at all.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.064
So after n months, you owe thirty thousand

00:03:21.244 --> 00:03:23.647
times one point zero zero six to the

00:03:23.907 --> 00:03:23.987
n,

00:03:24.528 --> 00:03:26.490
minus six hundred times a sum:

00:03:27.171 --> 00:03:29.874
one, plus one point zero zero six, plus

00:03:30.094 --> 00:03:32.016
one point zero zero six squared,

00:03:32.557 --> 00:03:34.299
up to the power n minus one.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.424
It's a geometric series with first term one,

00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:40.850
ratio one point zero zero six, and n

00:03:40.932 --> 00:03:41.271
terms.

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.373
Its sum is one point zero zero six

00:03:44.535 --> 00:03:46.114
to the n, minus one,

00:03:46.676 --> 00:03:49.136
all over one point zero zero six minus

00:03:49.297 --> 00:03:51.858
one, which is zero point zero zero six.

00:03:52.579 --> 00:03:55.233
Notice the ratio is one plus r, not

00:03:55.436 --> 00:03:55.877
r itself.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.325
In general, A sub n equals P times

00:03:59.526 --> 00:04:02.050
one plus r to the n, minus M

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.174
times one plus r to the n, minus

00:04:04.374 --> 00:04:05.436
one, all over r.

00:04:06.219 --> 00:04:07.344
Read it as two pieces.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:09.596
The first is what the loan would grow

00:04:09.656 --> 00:04:11.867
to with compound interest and no repayments.

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:15.115
The second is the repayments, each grown by

00:04:15.215 --> 00:04:17.339
interest from the month it was paid, because

00:04:17.379 --> 00:04:19.543
paying it stopped that much debt from growing.

00:04:20.227 --> 00:04:21.894
What you owe is the difference.

00:04:22.619 --> 00:04:25.047
For three months it gives twenty-eight thousand, seven

00:04:25.088 --> 00:04:27.777
hundred and thirty-two dollars forty-two, the same as

00:04:27.798 --> 00:04:28.179
the table.

00:04:28.647 --> 00:04:31.010
Now zoom out to a home loan: four

00:04:31.051 --> 00:04:33.254
hundred thousand dollars at five per cent a

00:04:33.335 --> 00:04:37.400
year, compounded monthly, repaid over thirty years at

00:04:37.481 --> 00:04:40.485
two thousand one hundred and forty-seven dollars twenty-nine

00:04:40.506 --> 00:04:40.806
a month.

00:04:41.368 --> 00:04:43.874
In the first month, more than three quarters

00:04:43.955 --> 00:04:45.639
of the repayment is interest.

00:04:46.101 --> 00:04:48.369
So the balance falls slowly at first, then

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:49.412
faster and faster.

00:04:50.015 --> 00:04:52.322
You don't owe less than half until about

00:04:52.423 --> 00:04:53.104
twenty years.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:55.785
Here's a way to remember each month of

00:04:55.826 --> 00:04:56.148
a loan.

00:04:56.654 --> 00:04:57.701
Grow, then pay.

00:04:58.466 --> 00:05:00.893
The balance grows by the interest, times one

00:05:00.914 --> 00:05:03.201
plus r, and then the repayment comes off,

00:05:03.804 --> 00:05:04.325
minus M.

00:05:06.996 --> 00:05:07.559
Your turn.

00:05:08.406 --> 00:05:10.893
A loan of twelve thousand dollars has interest

00:05:11.014 --> 00:05:13.602
at six per cent a year, compounded monthly.

00:05:14.145 --> 00:05:16.212
It's repaid at two hundred and fifty dollars

00:05:16.233 --> 00:05:16.713
a month.

00:05:17.598 --> 00:05:19.448
How much is owed after two months?

00:05:20.296 --> 00:05:21.369
Pause here to answer.

00:05:31.996 --> 00:05:33.872
The monthly rate is half a per cent.

00:05:34.376 --> 00:05:36.741
After one month, the balance is twelve thousand

00:05:36.862 --> 00:05:39.547
and sixty, minus two hundred and fifty, which

00:05:39.608 --> 00:05:41.290
is eleven thousand eight hundred and ten.

00:05:42.173 --> 00:05:44.755
After two months, it's eleven thousand six hundred

00:05:44.776 --> 00:05:46.596
and nineteen dollars and five cents.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.088
Eleven thousand five hundred is wrong.

00:05:49.491 --> 00:05:51.484
It takes off two repayments, but forgets the

00:05:51.565 --> 00:05:52.571
interest added each month.

00:05:54.162 --> 00:05:54.546
Last one.

00:05:55.391 --> 00:05:58.217
A loan of fifty thousand dollars has interest

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:00.201
at four point eight per cent a year,

00:06:00.521 --> 00:06:03.527
compounded monthly, with repayments of nine hundred dollars

00:06:03.547 --> 00:06:03.968
a month.

00:06:04.629 --> 00:06:06.552
Show that the amount owing after n months

00:06:06.832 --> 00:06:09.497
is fifty thousand times one point zero zero

00:06:09.557 --> 00:06:11.600
four to the n, minus two hundred and

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:14.505
twenty-five thousand, times one point zero zero four

00:06:14.785 --> 00:06:16.007
to the n, minus one.

00:06:16.731 --> 00:06:17.457
Pause here to answer.

00:06:28.034 --> 00:06:30.919
The repayments give nine hundred times a geometric

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:33.865
series with ratio one point zero zero four

00:06:34.047 --> 00:06:35.008
and n terms.

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.811
Its sum is one point zero zero four

00:06:37.852 --> 00:06:40.533
to the n, minus one, over zero point

00:06:40.554 --> 00:06:41.434
zero zero four,

00:06:42.035 --> 00:06:44.356
and nine hundred over zero point zero zero

00:06:44.397 --> 00:06:46.758
four is two hundred and twenty-five thousand.

00:06:47.561 --> 00:06:49.553
Using zero point zero zero four as the

00:06:49.594 --> 00:06:50.539
ratio is wrong.

00:06:50.902 --> 00:06:52.771
The ratio is one plus r.

00:06:54.401 --> 00:06:57.847
So a reducing-balance loan is compound interest with

00:06:57.988 --> 00:06:59.831
a repayment taken off every period,

00:07:00.392 --> 00:07:02.917
and its balance falls slowly at first, then

00:07:02.998 --> 00:07:03.398
faster.

00:07:04.301 --> 00:07:06.650
Here's the home loan again, cleared in thirty

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:06.951
years.

00:07:07.774 --> 00:07:09.861
What if you paid two thousand five hundred

00:07:09.881 --> 00:07:10.965
dollars a month instead?

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.137
How much sooner would it be gone?

00:07:15.928 --> 00:07:16.791
Here are the key notes.

00:07:17.194 --> 00:07:18.741
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:18.783 --> 00:07:19.244
to copy them.
